window.ASSASSINSCREED={"id":"assassinscreed","title":"Assassin’s Creed","subtitle":"Chronological Timeline","description":"Games · DLC · Books · Comics","color":"#c0202f","glow":"rgba(192,32,47,.35)","notes":"<p class=\"intro-lead\">If you&#x27;re here it&#x27;s either because you did some of the games and want to discover the lore of Assassin&#x27;s Creed or you&#x27;re absolutely sure to love this universe before even trying it. If you just want to discover the games in chronological order uncheck the rest, all other medias are bonus content (some very important). This guide is spoiler free like the others.</p><div class=\"intro-tags\"><span class=\"itag\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg>This guide works best for first-time plays.</span></div><div class=\"keys-title\">How to read this</div><div class=\"keys\"><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M8 2v4M16 2v4M3 10h18\"/></svg>The calendar</div><p>The saga happens in &quot;our&quot; world so we&#x27;ll count in years like we do.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7\"/><path d=\"M3 4v5h5M12 8v5l3 2\"/></svg>Flashbacks and flashforwards</div><p>Some events work better as a FLASHBACK because they spoil details from the games or gives your character an unnatural omniscience that can break immersion. There are also some FLASHFORWARDS because the events of the past are a lot more important compared to the present day framing.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 4h16v16H4z\"/><path d=\"M4 9h16M9 9v11\"/></svg>Games order</div><p>Most of the games have a present timeline but the core of the games all happen in the past.</p><p>This guide in based on the present timeline, we will go back and forth in history many times but it makes more sense like this.</p></div></div><details class=\"cuts\"><summary>What&#x27;s left out and why?<span class=\"n\">7 entries</span><svg class=\"chev\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"cuts-body\"><dl class=\"cuts-list\"><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Mobile and web games (Pirates, Identity, Rebellion...)</dt><dd>Not available anymore or non-canon</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Game novelizations</dt><dd>it&#x27;s a game based timeline but if you just want to read replace all the games by their official novelization.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Les Deux Royaumes comics</dt><dd>All the parts in the present are non-canon, the parts in the past are probably canon, you read them when you want keeping this in mind.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The Ming Storm and The Desert Threat</dt><dd>Not canon.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Blade of Shao Jun</dt><dd>It&#x27;s a manga adaptation of Chronicles China with a new modern times story and is considered canon but it doesn&#x27;t make sense storywise.. if you want to read it, it happens after Odyssey&#x27;s last DLC.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The roleplaying game</dt><dd>Too  hard to fit in the timeline but adds a lot of lore.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The chinese books</dt><dd>Unless you speak chinese...</dd></div></dl></div></details>","eras":[{"title":"Altaïr Saga","phase":"SAGA 1","ink":1,"entries":[{"id":"ac-game-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"4729","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed","date":"1191","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/0bc/0bcc108295a244b488d5c25f7d867220.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-altairs-chronicles-1","type":"jeu","level":"bonus","tmdb":"24789","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Altaïr's Chronicles","date":"1190","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/bca/bca12cc8adb162b46a0b5a1296f3846a.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"faq":{"animus":"Probably Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-bloodlines-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"5160","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Bloodlines","date":"1191-1193","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/071/0711f22aeaf7927ccd071b186743ca5e.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"}]},{"title":"Ezio Saga","phase":"SAGA 2","ink":2,"entries":[{"id":"ac-lineage-1","type":"video","level":"important","tmdb":"1008421","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Lineage","date":"1476","img":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/pZFyU0aGyi3uinGEhfXbX9vbik4.jpg","desc":"Assassin's Creed: Lineage is a series of three short films based on the universe of the video game Assassin's Creed, created by Ubisoft. The first episode was released on 26 October 2009 via YouTube, and the final two episodes were released on 12 November 2009 on Spike TV, before being later uploaded to YouTube for international viewing purposes."},{"id":"ac-ii-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"28568","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed II","date":"1476-1488","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/1be/1bed7fae69d1004c09dfe1101d5a3a94.jpg","notes":["Until end of Sequence 12 (Battle of Forli)","I highly recommend you to complete the optional 20 hidden glyphs but if you don't like collectibles look for \"The Truth\" video on YouTube when you completed the game it's pretty important !"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-ii-discovery-1","type":"jeu","level":"bonus","tmdb":"26200","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed II: Discovery","date":"1491-1492","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/88f/88f9c892952f8e12df54090e79ad8b51.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Probably Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-ii-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"28568","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed II","date":"1497-1499","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/1be/1bed7fae69d1004c09dfe1101d5a3a94.jpg","notes":["Bonfire of the Vanities and endgame","I highly recommend you to complete the optional 20 hidden glyphs but if you don't like collectibles look for \"The Truth\" video on YouTube when you completed the game it's pretty important !"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-ascendance-1","type":"video","level":"bonus","tmdb":"57051","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Ascendance","date":"1502","img":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/fxSoGWqHTGPlEilOVhQaAJcSAZS.jpg","desc":"Assassins Creed: Ascendance is a short, animated film project created to expand the Assassin's Creed series. Created as a bridge between Assassin's Creed II and Assassin's Creed: Brotherhood, the short film details more of Cesare Borgia's rise to power."},{"id":"ac-brotherhood-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"10064","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Brotherhood","date":"1499-1503","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/116/116b93c6876a361a96b2eee3ee58ab13.jpg","notes":["Until end of Sequence 8 (The Borgia)"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-the-da-vinci-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"40751","media":"game","title":"The Da Vinci Disappearance","date":"1506","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/bbe/bbeea9a20ece3dbbdb81045243d50569.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-brotherhood-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"10064","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Brotherhood","date":"1507","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/116/116b93c6876a361a96b2eee3ee58ab13.jpg","notes":["Endgame"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-the-secret-crusade-1","type":"roman","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin’s Creed: The Secret Crusade","date":"1258","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10240406-L.jpg","notes":["It's the in-universe book that Ezio is reading at the beginning of Revelations, it retells events from Altaïr's saga but adds much more."],"desc":"Niccolò Polo, father of Marco, will finally reveal the story he has kept secret all his life – the story of Altaïr, one of the Brotherhood's most extraordinary assassins. Altaïr embarks on a formidable mission – one that takes him throughout the Holy Land and shows him the true meaning of the Assassin's Creed. To demonstrate his commitment, Altaïr must defeat nine deadly enemies, including the Templar leader, Robert de Sablé."},{"id":"ac-revelations-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"4358","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Revelations","date":"1511-1512","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/193/19390fa5e75e9048b22c9a736cf9992f.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-brotherhood-revelations-animi-1","type":"video","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Brotherhood & Revelations - Animi Training Program","date":"","notes":["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ah2XSXZqrcA"],"desc":"The Animi Training Program was a secret Templar initiative to train Abstergo Industries employees in the skills they needed to fight against the remnants of the Assassins, such as combat and freerunning, through the use of the Animus, a device created by Abstergo that allowed a person to relive genetic memories.","faq":{"animus":"Juhani Otso Berg"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-the-lost-archive-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"42008","media":"game","title":"The Lost Archive","date":"","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/703/703b74e926dd91cfeab6439c12e2a868.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2007-2012"},{"id":"ac-embers-1","type":"video","level":"must","tmdb":"79089","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Embers","date":"1524","img":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/6aeKG4ko7hAd80sakNw49ktrcPE.jpg","desc":"Now living in a cozy Tuscan Villa with his wife and their two children, Ezio spends his time enjoying the company of family, old friends, and cultivating his vineyards. The life of this former Assassin Mentor will not stay quiet for long. One day, a mysterious Assassin shows up at Ezio's door quite unexpectedly, begging for Ezio's aid. Will this old Assassin's fire die out before he can save the ones he loves, or will it burn brightly one last time?"},{"id":"ac-chronicles-china-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"20180","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed Chronicles: China","date":"1526-1532","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c5a/c5a362394197a5aa0cb8371a62154c8b.jpg","tags":["flashforward"],"notes":["So... these games don't have present time parts but still happen much later... We will not bother about that for now. I highly recommend you to complete the optional 3 hidden Assassin logos (in the 3 Chronicles games) to unlock a secret ending cinematic in the last game but we will come back to it much later."],"faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-the-fall-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Fall","date":"1888-1918","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Assassin's Creed: The Fall is a 2010-2011 comic book written by Cameron Stewart and Karl Kerschl. A sequel comic book entitled Assassin's Creed: The Chain, again following the lives of Daniel Cross and Nikolai Orelov, was announced after San Diego Comic-Con 2011 and released in late July 2012.","faq":{"animus":"Daniel Cross"},"present":"1998-2000"},{"id":"ac-chronicles-russia-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"19338","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed Chronicles: Russia","date":"1918","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/cd9/cd9a44c7a80b8319a84ea737e71cb592.jpg","tags":["flashforward"],"notes":["So... these games don't have present time parts but still happen much later (and this one is the last one but we play it now). We will not bother about that for now. I highly recommend you to complete the optional 3 hidden Assassin logos (in the 3 Chronicles games) to unlock a secret ending cinematic in this game but we will come back to it much later."],"faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-the-chain-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Chain","date":"1919-1928","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Assassin's Creed: The Chain is a 2012 comic book, a sequel to Assassin's Creed: The Fall and the conclusion of the story of Nikolai Orelov. Whereas The Fall was first published by DC WildStorm as monthly comic issues, The Chain is only available to pre-order through Ubiworkshop.","faq":{"animus":"Daniel Cross"},"present":"2002"}]},{"title":"Kenway Saga","phase":"SAGA 3","ink":3,"entries":[{"id":"ac-iii-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"13305","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed III","date":"1754-1778","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/275/2759da6fcaa8f81f21800926168c85f6.jpg","notes":["Until end of Sequence 10 (Battle of Monmouth)"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-benedict-arnold-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"13305","media":"game","title":"Benedict Arnold","date":"1780","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/275/2759da6fcaa8f81f21800926168c85f6.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-iii-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"13305","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed III","date":"1781-1783","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/275/2759da6fcaa8f81f21800926168c85f6.jpg","notes":["Endgame"],"faq":{"animus":"Desmond Miles"},"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-iii-abstergo-hacked-1","type":"video","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed III - Abstergo Hacked","date":"","notes":["PART 1 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PyyKNAflqbw","PART 2 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YueCNPMnxZg"],"present":"2012"},{"id":"ac-the-tyranny-of-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"41990","media":"game","title":"The Tyranny of King Washington","date":"~1783","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/747/747534745faecec4625c755731351328_4vWj1p1.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-forsaken-1","type":"roman","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin’s Creed: Forsaken","date":"1735-1783","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10030535-L.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"1735 – London, Haytham Kenway has been taught to use a sword from the age he was able to hold one. When his family's house is attacked – his father murdered and his sister taken by armed men, Haytham defends his home the only way he can: he kills. With no family, he is taken in by a mysterious tutor who trains him to become a deadly killer. Consumed by his thirst for revenge, Haytham begins a quest for retribution, trusting no one and questioning everything he has ever known."},{"id":"ac-iii-liberation-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"4209","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed III: Liberation","date":"1765-1777","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/e20/e20a9d3e14560dfd90e1713211af2dc5.jpg","notes":["I highly recommend you to complete all the optional Citizen E glitchs to unlock the real end of the game but if you don't like to do this look at the video just beneath when you completed the game it's pretty important !","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ynl8fYAO-EQ&t=192s"],"faq":{"animus":"Random Helix customer"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-iv-black-flag-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"1017360","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed IV: Black Flag - Aveline","date":"1784","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/990/99088f6f170459244defd7afd9fce096.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-iv-black-flag-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"3841","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed IV: Black Flag","date":"1715-1722","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/849/849414b978db37d4563ff9e4b0d3a787.jpg","notes":["Not Resynced !!! (yet...)"],"faq":{"animus":"Abstergo employee \"Noob\""},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-iv-black-flag-3","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed IV Black Flag: Blackbeard – The Lost Journal","date":"1713-1718","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Few moments in history have proven as timelessly fascinating as the lawless Golden Age of Piracy, which was largely played out in the Caribbean of the 16th and early 17th centuries. In this time of rebellion, fortune, intrigue, and adventure, Blackbeard stands as one of the most fearsome captains to have ever sailed the seas."},{"id":"ac-freedom-cry-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"42466","media":"game","title":"Freedom Cry","date":"1735-1737","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/d03/d0398a47e8d88cc160050217172bc8f2.jpg","notes":["Also available in a standalone game titled Assassin's Creed: Freedom Cry"],"faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-brahman-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Brahman","date":"1839","desc":"Who is Jot Soora? Devoted fiancé of movie star Monima Das, gifted programmer at software giant MysoreTech, or deadly Assassin with a secret? When Jot stumbles into a layer of code deep in his company's new device, the discovery threatens his relationship, his job and his life. it also reveals shocking links to an ancestral past that cause him to question everything he knows about himself.","faq":{"animus":"Jot Soora"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-chronicles-india-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"19274","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed Chronicles: India","date":"1841","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/e99/e9969ab76756fe041aaa72cdeb768649.jpg","tags":["flashforward"],"notes":["So... these games don't have present time parts but still happen much later... We will not bother about that for now. I highly recommend you to complete the optional 3 hidden Assassin logos (in the 3 Chronicles games) to unlock a secret ending cinematic in the last game but we will come back to it much later so don't watch it now."],"faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-templars-black-cross-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin’s Creed: Templars - Black Cross","date":"1927","desc":"In 1927, Darius Gift, young, handsome, terribly entitled, is given his first mission for the ancient Templar Order, and the chance to clear his tarnished family name. All doesn't quite go to plan when he arrives in Shanghai, however, and his inexperience jeopardizes the whole operation. Thankfully, he isn't the only Templar new to the city, as the enigmatic Black Cross is stalking the shadows... and saving Darius from failure!","faq":{"animus":"Juhani Otso Berg"},"present":"2013"},{"id":"ac-fcbd-2016-great-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed FCBD 2016 - Great Wall","date":"1927","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Enter the shadowy world of the Assassins and Templars, two feuding factions who have battled over the centuries to decide the course of humanity! Two all-new short stories, written and illustrated by the creative teams of the regular comics, highlight a shocking event in the life of new Assassin Charlotte de la Cruz, and reveal the true extent of the mysterious Templar Black Cross's terrifying skills!"},{"id":"ac-rogue-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"17545","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Rogue","date":"1752-1760","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/3c4/3c4a44ed99c87c56e0cdcfaaaf5c3628.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Abstergo employee \"Numbskull\""},"present":"2014"}]},{"title":"Helix & Abstergo Saga","phase":"SAGA 4","ink":4,"entries":[{"id":"ac-unity-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"8146","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Unity","date":"1789-1794","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/59f/59fc1c5de1d29cb9234741c97d250150.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2014"},{"id":"ac-unity-abstergo-entertainment-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed Unity: Abstergo Entertainment: Employee Handbook","date":"","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Crafted to resemble a set of Abstergo case files, this immersive and interactive book provides a glimpse into the technology that allows characters to inhabit the lives of their ancestors — a cornerstone of the Assassin's Creed narrative.","faq":{"animus":"Robert Fraser"},"present":"2014"},{"id":"ac-dead-kings-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"42950","media":"game","title":"Dead Kings","date":"1794","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a75/a75a893fc77d4b7c9b581eeea052d024.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2014"},{"id":"ac-syndicate-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"42895","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Syndicate","date":"1868","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/9f1/9f189c639f70f91166df415811a8b525.jpg","notes":["Until end of Sequence 9 (Shall We Dance?)"],"faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-the-last-maharaja-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"43652","media":"game","title":"The Last Maharaja","date":"1868","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/8cd/8cdeb19c3004ea5a4ba141cb8f61fa30.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-syndicate-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"42895","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Syndicate","date":"1868","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/9f1/9f189c639f70f91166df415811a8b525.jpg","notes":["Endgame"],"faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-jack-the-ripper-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"43541","media":"game","title":"Jack the Ripper","date":"1888","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/d4e/d4e38c7a04e378903dd4ece1f4b3087b.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Helix Initiate"},"present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-chronicles-russia-secret-1","type":"video","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed Chronicles: Russia - Secret Ending","date":"","notes":["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0JKrEU7o1Nk"],"desc":"The game follows Nikolai Orelov in Russia in 1918, taking place between the events of the comic Assassin's Creed: The Fall and Assassin's Creed: The Chain. As the final installment in the Assassin's Creed Chronicles series, the game differs stylistically from most previous entries in the franchise, being set on a 2.5D plane like Assassin's Creed II: Discovery.","present":"2015"},{"id":"ac-underworld-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin’s Creed: Underworld","date":"1847-1868","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7794980-L.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"A disgraced Assassin. A deep-cover agent. A quest for redemption. 1862, and with London in the grip of the Industrial Revolution, the world's first underground railway is under construction. When a body is discovered at the dig, it sparks the beginning of the latest deadly chapter in the centuries-old battle between the Assassins and Templars."},{"id":"ac-the-engine-of-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Engine of History – The Magus Conspiracy","date":"1851-1862","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"The war between Assassins and Templars wreaks havoc in the Victorian era, in this breakneck thriller which opens up a whole new chapter of the Assassin’s Creed universe London, 1851 — When Pierrette, daring acrobat performing at the Great Exhibition, rescues the mathematician Ada Lovelace from a gang of thugs, she becomes immersed in an ancient feud between Assassins and Templars."},{"id":"ac-the-engine-of-2","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Engine of History – The Resurrection Plot","date":"1869-1889","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"The conspiracies of the Templars reverberate across nineteenth century Europe as they seize control of the future, and only the Brotherhood of Assassins can hold them back, in this globetrotting adventure from Assassin's Creed. Cairo, 1869. When a bomb goes off at the Khedivial Opera House celebrating the opening of the new Suez Canal, visiting Assassin Pierrette Arnaud investigates, only to uncover a plot to eradicate free will..."},{"id":"ac-assassins-trial-by-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Assassins - Trial by Fire","date":"1692","desc":"The first stunning arc of the Assassin's Creed series collected. New initiate Charlotte de la Cruz ventures into the Animus, and the genetic memories of her ancestor, Tom Stoddard, to discover the truth about the hidden world of the Assassins and Templars and the feud that spans centuries.","faq":{"animus":"Charlotte de la Cruz"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-fcbd-2016-the-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed FCBD 2016 - The Chair","date":"1791","desc":"Enter the shadowy world of the Assassins and Templars, two feuding factions who have battled over the centuries to decide the course of humanity! Two all-new short stories, written and illustrated by the creative teams of the regular comics, highlight a shocking event in the life of new Assassin Charlotte de la Cruz, and reveal the true extent of the mysterious Templar Black Cross's terrifying skills!","faq":{"animus":"Charlotte de la Cruz"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-assassins-setting-sun-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Assassins - Setting Sun","date":"1536","desc":"Collecting the second arc of the critically-acclaimed Assassin's Creed comics, Setting Sun sees Charlotte searching for a clue that will help the Assassins on their quest to foil the Templar's plans. Hidden deep in the memories of her Inca ancestor lies a word that will save them – if it's not too late! Collects Assassin’s Creed: Assassin’s #6-10","faq":{"animus":"Charlotte de la Cruz"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-assassins-homecoming-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Assassins - Homecoming","date":"1515-1516","desc":"The Brotherhood of the Assassins is in trouble. Resources depleted by their long feud with the Templar Order, faced with a world where the goalposts are constantly shifting, they can only struggle to regain their footing. A mysterious collective offers an alliance, but is this third faction a golden opportunity? Or a Faustian bargain? Join Charlotte de la Cruz and Galina Voronina as they try and navigate a clear path for the Assassins through turbulent waters!","faq":{"animus":"Charlotte de la Cruz"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-templars-cross-of-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Templars - Cross of War","date":"1805-1808","desc":"Collects the incredible second arc of the riveting Black Cross saga! In the dungeons of Tripoli, a man will have his fortunes changed forever as he becomes an agent of honor for the legendary Templar Order! The introduction of the second character ever to be officially called the Black Cross, defender of the Templar Order ideals!","faq":{"animus":"Juhani Otso Berg"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-last-descendants-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Last Descendants","date":"1863","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10307010-L.jpg","desc":"Nothing in Owen's life has been right since his father died in prison, accused of a crime Owen is certain he didn't commit. Monroe, the IT guy at school, might finally bring Owen the means to clear his father's name by letting him use an Animus — a device that lets users explore the genetic memories buried within their own DNA. The experience brings Owen more than he bargained for.","faq":{"animus":"Owen Meyers"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-last-descendants-locus-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Last Descendants - Locus","date":"1872","desc":"Assassin's Creed: Last Descendants – Locus, otherwise simply known as Locus, is a comic book miniseries published by Titan Comics. A tie-in to the Last Descendants young adult book series as well as a return to the Victorian era London setting of Assassin's Creed: Syndicate, the comic is written by Ian Edginton and illustrated by Caspar Wijngaard.","faq":{"animus":"Sean Molloy"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-heresy-1","type":"roman","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Heresy","date":"1429","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8908572-L.jpg","desc":"The new book set in the universe of Assassin's Creed. Reliving the memories of his ancestor who fought beside Joan of Arc, high-ranking Templar Simon Hathaway slowly uncovers secrets of the past that could dangerously impact his present... and that of the entire Templar order. An endless conflict. An old wrong. A new revelation.","faq":{"animus":"Simon Hathaway"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-movie-1","type":"film","level":"important","tmdb":"121856","media":"movie","title":"Assassin's Creed","date":"1492","img":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/kDXewoEcvbn0pUvJ8W3vfkuWgHw.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Callum Lynch"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-last-descendants-tomb-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Last Descendants – Tomb of the Khan","date":"1259","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14526312-L.jpg","notes":["Happens in parallel of the movie"],"desc":"Owen and his friends have lost. They managed to do something incredible, but were defeated nonetheless. When they located the first piece of an ancient and powerful relic long considered a legend-the Trident of Eden -it seemed little could stop them. This piece was sought by the Brotherhood of Assassins and the Templar Order, but before either organization could take the piece, it was stolen by an unknown third party.","faq":{"animus":"Owen Meyers"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-last-descendants-fate-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Last Descendants – Fate of the Gods","date":"985","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10307010-L.jpg","notes":["Happens in parallel of the movie"],"desc":"The stunning conclusion to the Last Descendants Trilogy! Only one piece of the Trident of Eden remains - Isaiah, a rogue Templar agent, has discovered both the faith prong and the fear prong of this powerful relic. Should he possess the devotion prong, there is little that can stop him. For the time being, Owen and his fellow teens have established an uneasy alliance across Assassin and Templar lines in order to stop Isaiah while they still can.","faq":{"animus":"Owen Meyers"},"present":"2016"},{"id":"ac-reflections-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Reflections","date":"1227-1796","desc":"Assassin's Creed: Reflections is a comic book miniseries published by Titan Comics to mark the franchise's tenth anniversary.","faq":{"animus":"Juhani Otso Berg"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-uprising-common-ground-1","type":"comic","level":"must","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Uprising - Common Ground","date":"","desc":"A game-changing new chapter in the ongoing Assassin's Creed saga! With the Phoenix Project nearing its completion, tensions are running high for both the Brotherhood and the Templar Order. A new world order is on the horizon and only Charlotte and her new allies have the knowledge and skill to save humanity from subjugation!","present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-uprising-inflection-point-1","type":"comic","level":"must","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Uprising - Inflection Point","date":"1927-1937","desc":"The Phoenix project saga begins to unravel in this second thrilling chapter of Assassin’s Creed Uprising! Our modern day Assassins take the fight to the heart of the Spanish Civil War in order to secure a valuable artifact that could change the course of history. But when a brand new enemy rears its ugly head, both the Brotherhood and Templar Order are forced to form a shaky alliance.","faq":{"animus":"Charlotte de la Cruz"},"present":"2017"}]},{"title":"Layla Hassan Saga","phase":"SAGA 5","ink":5,"entries":[{"id":"ac-origins-desert-oath-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed Origins: Desert Oath","date":"70-56 BC","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8874067-L.jpg","desc":"Before Assassin's Creed: Origins, there was an Oath. Egypt, 70BC, a merciless killer stalks the land. His mission: to find and destroy the last members of an ancient order, the Medjay — to eradicate the bloodline. In peaceful Siwa, the town's protector abruptly departs, leaving his teenage son, Bayek, with questions about his own future and a sense of purpose he knows he must fulfill."},{"id":"ac-origins-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"28153","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Origins","date":"49-43 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/336/336c6bd63d83cf8e59937ab8895d1240.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-the-hidden-ones-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"320365","media":"game","title":"The Hidden Ones","date":"38 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/10f/10ff47ddc11eab13260c65144447ea60.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-the-curse-of-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"320364","media":"game","title":"The Curse of the Pharaohs","date":"34 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/27b/27b82ac09d93c3a85147e2ee7365c1a3.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-origins-2","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Origins","date":"30 BC","desc":"The player takes on the role of a Medjay named Bayek and his wife Aya, as they work to protect the people of the Ptolemaic Kingdom during a time of widespread upheaval: the Pharaoh, Ptolemy XIII, struggles to maintain his rule whilst harboring ambitions of expanding his kingdom; his sister, the recently deposed Queen Cleopatra, begins marshalling loyalist forces to launch a counter-coup against Ptolemy; and frequent incursions into the Kingdom by the Roman Republic under the command of Julius Caesar lead to fears of an imminent invasion."},{"id":"ac-conspiracies-die-glocke-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Conspiracies - Die Glocke","date":"1940-1943","desc":"New era - New adventure - New Assassin. Europe, World War II. On the sidelines of the race for the atomic bomb, discover the story of Eddie Gorm and his integration into the Assassin Brotherhood while he infiltrates the Templars to foil their plan to create a devastating weapon. Eddie Gorm is the boss of the docks and his only obsession is to run his small business.","faq":{"animus":"Maxime Gorm"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-conspiracies-project-rainbow-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Conspiracies - Project Rainbow","date":"1943","desc":"April 1939, Nazi Germany launch a race against the Allies to build the first nuclear bomb. Soon, Colonel Boris Pash, a member of the Assassin Brotherhood, discovers that the Nazi program is only a decoy to divert the attention of the Allies. Hitler is actually looking for a far superior and striking power, thanks in particular to a mysterious weapon: Die Glocke.","faq":{"animus":"Maxime Gorm"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-bloodstone-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Bloodstone","date":"1957-1964","desc":"The secret struggle between Assassins and Templars hits the Vietnam War! Part one of a new thriller set in the world of Assassin's Creed, from Guillaume Dorison ( Assassin's Creed: Conspiracies, Devil May Cry ) and artist Ennio Bufi ( They Made History ). Tomo, one of the youngest members of the Japanese Assassin cell, has uncovered a conspiracy.","faq":{"animus":"Tomo Sakagawa"},"present":"2017"},{"id":"ac-uprising-finale-1","type":"comic","level":"must","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Uprising - Finale","date":"","desc":"The final chapter of Assassin's Creed: Uprising concludes the Phoenix Project Saga in epic fashion – the end of a ten-year storyline straight from the video games! Time has run out for our modern-day assassins! While fan-favorite characters Juno, Otso Berg and Black Cross face the advent of a new world order, Charlotte and her cell confront the biggest threat the brotherhood has ever encountered... and not all of them will survive!","present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-odyssey-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Odyssey","date":"431-429 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","notes":["Kassandra is the canon character so you should play her","Until end of Unified Front memory"],"faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-legacy-of-the-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"799250","media":"game","title":"Legacy of the First Blade - Hunted","date":"~429 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a7a/a7a6e06615c119685e4e0f0412653505.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-odyssey-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Odyssey","date":"429-426 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","notes":["Until end of A Blood Feast memory"],"faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-legacy-of-the-2","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"799250","media":"game","title":"Legacy of the First Blade - Shadow Heritage","date":"~426 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a7a/a7a6e06615c119685e4e0f0412653505.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-legacy-of-the-3","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"799250","media":"game","title":"Legacy of the First Blade - Bloodline","date":"~425 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/a7a/a7a6e06615c119685e4e0f0412653505.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-odyssey-3","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Odyssey","date":"425-421 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","notes":["Until end of Atlantis Destroyed memory"],"faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-odyssey-the-lost-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Odyssey - The Lost Tales of Greece: The Heir of Memories","date":"421 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-odyssey-4","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Odyssey","date":"425-421 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","notes":["Endgame"],"faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-the-fate-of-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"406952","media":"game","title":"The Fate of Atlantis","date":"~421 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c95/c9565c19c24cd13875572cc26e62bef3.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-those-who-are-1","type":"dlc","level":"must","tmdb":"58616","media":"game","title":"Those Who Are Treasured","date":"421-420 BC","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/c6b/c6bd26767c1053fef2b10bb852943559.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2018"},{"id":"ac-gold-1","type":"audio","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Gold","date":"1696","desc":"Assassin's Creed: Gold is a stand-alone tale from the Assassin's Creed universe in which we meet Aliyah Khan, a card shark and hustler, who's been dealt a rough hand in life. Surviving through her smarts and street scams, Aliyah struggles to get by until she loses big time to a mysterious older man, Gavin Banks. Her only option to repay Banks is to become an Assassin.","present":"2019"},{"id":"ac-valhalla-song-of-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – Song of Glory","date":"870","desc":"A Tale from the Saga of a Viking Warrior Blades clash in this prequel to Ubisoft's next hit video game, Assassin’s Creed Valhalla. Written by Cavan Scott ( Star Wars Adventures, Vikings ), illustrated by Martin Tunica, and colored by Michael Atiyeh ( The Orville, Dragon Age: Blue Wraith ), Assassin’s Creed Valhalla: Song of Glory takes readers back to a Mid-9th Century Norway. Eivor, a Viking warrior, observes a village raided by a neighboring kingdom."},{"id":"ac-valhalla-1","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"437059","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla","date":"872-878","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/934/9346092ae11bf7582c883869468171cc.jpg","notes":["As seen in the comic, woman Eivor is the canon character","Don't forget to do the important quest A Fated Encounter on the isle of Skye while doing the game","I highly recommend you to complete the optional 10 Animus anomalies but if you don't like them look for \"The Hidden Truth\" video on YouTube when you completed the game it's pretty important !"],"faq":{"animus":"Layla Hassan"},"present":"2020"},{"id":"ac-valhalla-blood-brothers-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – Blood Brothers","date":"~866","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14685900-L.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"notes":["Read it after the main game or while playing after meeting Ivarr and Halfdan"],"desc":"Not long before the exploits of Eivor Wolf-Kissed, Jarl Stensson and his [sons], Ulf and Björn, make their way to England at the behest of Halfdan Ragnarsson and Ivarr the Boneless. Filled with excitement, confidence and bloodlust, the [two] brothers are eager to go to war against Aelfred the Great and his Anglo Saxon army. But they would do well not to underestimate what awaits them on those green shores..."},{"id":"ac-valhalla-geirmunds-saga-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – Geirmund's Saga","date":"867-878","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12786127-L.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"notes":["Read it after the main game or while playing after the East Anglia alliance arc"],"desc":"Discover the epic tale of legendary viking Geirmund Hel-hide in this new novel set in the world of Assassin's Creed Valhalla Mid-9th Century CE. The Viking attacks and invasions are shattering England’s kingdoms. Born into a royal lineage of Norwegian kings, Geirmund Hel-hide sets out for adventure to prove his worth as a Viking and a warrior."},{"id":"ac-valhalla-the-hidden-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – The Hidden Codex","date":"~878","desc":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – The Hidden Codex is a bande dessinée graphic novel by the same artists behind Assassin's Creed: Valhalla' s tie-in webcomic."},{"id":"ac-valhalla-sword-of-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla – Sword of the White Horse","date":"878","desc":"A Celtic warrior defending her people from Viking raiders infiltrates an ancient sect to save her homeland, in this gripping original saga set in the world of Assassin's Creed Valhalla. Mercia, 878. Witch-warrior Niamh discovers a new order called the Hidden Ones is seeking to establish a foothold in Lunden. Her land is already scarred by Viking raiders, bloody wars, and clashing cultures."},{"id":"ac-wrath-of-the-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"595182","media":"game","title":"Wrath of the Druids","date":"879-882","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/5c4/5c485e1593cadce3236886181ea5658a.jpg","notes":["Accessible early but happens after the end of the main story in the past but not in the present"],"faq":{"animusSpoiler":"Probably Basim"},"present":"2020"},{"id":"ac-the-siege-of-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"799246","media":"game","title":"The Siege of Paris","date":"885-887","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/ec1/ec17b473d4ac3954a0ba55c0c6254694.jpg","notes":["Accessible early but happens after the end of the main story in the past but not in the present"],"faq":{"animusSpoiler":"Probably Basim"},"present":"2020"},{"id":"ac-valhalla-forgotten-myths-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla - Forgotten Myths","date":"~2306 IE","desc":"Thor, Baldr, and Heimdall have discovered trouble lurking at Asgard's borders once again. A mighty fire giant from Muspelheim is threatening the land of the Æsir. In the aftermath of the raging battle, Baldr discovers that the Muspels are now massing at the gates of Svartalfheim and begins a journey to bring peace to the realms."},{"id":"ac-dawn-of-ragnarok-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"799247","media":"game","title":"Dawn of Ragnarök","date":"~2306 IE","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/9e0/9e0faef5dbebecf5bc3aa101d73125c8.jpg","faq":{"animusSpoiler":"Probably Basim"},"present":"2020"},{"id":"ac-valhalla-2","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"437059","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Valhalla","date":"887","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/934/9346092ae11bf7582c883869468171cc.jpg","notes":["The Forgotten Saga free update + The Last Chapter epilogue"],"faq":{"animusSpoiler":"Basim"},"present":"2020"},{"id":"ac-escape-room-puzzle-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Escape Room Puzzle Book","date":"~431 BC-1480","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14562927-L.jpg","desc":"The Assassin's Creed Escape Room Puzzle Book is an exciting journey through history in which you must solve a series of puzzles and mysteries to save humanity. You are Joey, a museum worker who comes across a mysterious blade that sets in motion a chain of events that completely upends your life. Drawn into the world of the Assassins, you must tour through time and space — from 5th century BCE Greece to the catacombs of medieval Venice — in order to foil a malevolent Isu plot.","faq":{"animus":"Joey"},"present":"2022"},{"id":"ac-mirage-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"845261","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Mirage","date":"861","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/fbd/fbd0128013b7965904be571e75fb30c0.jpg","notes":["Until end of The Return memory"],"faq":{"animus":"Random Assassin"},"present":"2023"},{"id":"ac-valley-of-memories-1","type":"dlc","level":"bonus","tmdb":"845261","media":"game","title":"Valley of Memories","date":"862","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/fbd/fbd0128013b7965904be571e75fb30c0.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Random Assassin"},"present":"2023"},{"id":"ac-mirage-2","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"845261","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Mirage","date":"862","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/fbd/fbd0128013b7965904be571e75fb30c0.jpg","notes":["Endgame"],"faq":{"animus":"Random Assassin"},"present":"2023"},{"id":"ac-mirage-daughter-of-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Mirage – Daughter of No One","date":"819-824","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14713990-L.jpg","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Master Assassin Roshan's past is revealed in the hunt along the Silk Road for a powerful mysterious artifact in this essential Assassin's Creed adventure Cairo, 824 – In the bowels of prison, escape is out of the question. The best Roshan can hope for is a quick death. She certainly doesn't expect a second chance offered by a cloaked stranger who says Roshan is exactly what they need: Someone who can disappear, who will do what needs to be done, someone expendable..."},{"id":"ac-mirage-a-soar-1","type":"comic","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Mirage - A Soar of Eagles","date":"~855-861","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Years before the events of Assassin's Creed Mirage, a young Fuladh must return to his homeland to investigate political unrest that could point to a secret Order of the Ancients' stronghold. But in order to discover what's behind the chaos and violence in Adulis, Fuladh and Roshan will have to confront a more immediate danger."},{"id":"ac-the-golden-city-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Golden City","date":"867","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14135985-L.jpg","desc":"A young emperor's life hangs in the balance, and only the Brotherhood of Assassins can save him, in this action-packed historical adventure from the award-winning Assassin's Creed universe. Constantinople, 867 – A murderous plot is afoot. Assisted by the Order of the Ancients, the emperor schemes to assassinate his son and throw the city into chaos."},{"id":"ac-the-silk-road-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: The Silk Road","date":"870","desc":"Put yourself in the shoes of an Assassin and immerse yourself in a completely new interactive adventure. France, 870 CE. You play as Oisel, a young Assassin from the Chinon Bureau whose daily life is turned upside down upon receiving a strange letter from Basim, illustrious mentor of Constantinople. With your best friend, Matthias, and your loyal raptor, Alouette, you are sent on his tracks along the Silk Road. Your first stop: Antioch.","faq":{"animus":"Random Abstergo employee"}}]},{"title":"Animus Hub Saga","phase":"SAGA 6","ink":6,"entries":[{"id":"ac-forgotten-temple-1","type":"comic","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Forgotten Temple","date":"1724-1725","desc":"Edward Kenway returns to take the leap of faith in an all-new adventure. The high-seas hunt is on for a long-lost treasure left by Those Who Came Before. But this time, the Templars aren't the only ones after the prize. Join history's most cunning pirate in an epic journey around the Chinese Sea.","faq":{"animus":"Noa Kim"},"present":"2023"},{"id":"ac-nexus-vr-1","type":"jeu","level":"bonus","tmdb":"974464","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Nexus VR","date":"","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/166/166e0f484feabe29b016c05e82441284.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Undercover Assassin hacker"},"present":"2023"},{"id":"ac-shadows-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"981791","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Shadows","date":"1579-1582","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/526/526881e0f5f8c1550e51df3801f96ea3.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Animus EGO user"},"present":"~2081"},{"id":"ac-claws-of-awaji-1","type":"dlc","level":"important","tmdb":"1007217","media":"game","title":"Claws of Awaji","date":"~1585","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/902/902effe8e506327cd42c883f2ce4c6ef.jpg","faq":{"animus":"Animus EGO user"},"present":"~2081"},{"id":"ac-shadows-2","type":"jeu","level":"must","tmdb":"981791","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Shadows","date":"~1585","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/games/526/526881e0f5f8c1550e51df3801f96ea3.jpg","notes":["Black Tides epilogue"],"faq":{"animus":"Animus EGO user"},"present":"~2081"},{"id":"ac-shadows-tales-of-1","type":"roman","level":"important","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Shadows – Tales of Iga","date":"1541-1561","tags":["flashback"],"desc":"Assassin's Creed: Shadows – Tales of Iga (Japanese: アサシン クリード シャドウズ 伊賀の物語, Assassin's Creed: Shadows – Iga no Monogatari ) is an ongoing manga that has been released on Japan's Weekly Young Magazine website since 20 March 2025. The manga serves as a prequel to Assassin's Creed: Shadows and explores the backstories of Fujibayashi Nagato, Hattori Hanzō, and Tsuyu, who come together to fight against the growing Templar threat in Japan in 1560."},{"id":"ac-black-flag-resynced-1","type":"jeu","level":"important","tmdb":"1017360","media":"game","title":"Assassin's Creed: Black Flag Resynced","date":"1701-1722","img":"https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/990/99088f6f170459244defd7afd9fce096.jpg","notes":["So... think like this : after the events of present time in Black Flag, Abstergo rewrote Edward Kenway's story to release their version on the Animus Hub"],"faq":{"animus":"Animus EGO user"},"present":"~2096"}]},{"title":"Assassins Through History Saga","phase":"SAGA 7","ink":7,"entries":[{"id":"ac-dynasty-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Dynasty","date":"751-758","img":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14663065-L.jpg","desc":"In the 14th year of the Tianbao Era (CE 755) An Lushan, a military governor with ties to the Knights Templar, leads his elite corps to rebel against the Tang dynasty, and the ill-prepared Tang empire falters under the threat. As the Tang dynasty starts to crumble, Li E, a shady Assassin trained by the Hidden Ones in the far West, teams up with Tang loyalists to turn the tide and save both the dynasty and the country from this crisis."},{"id":"ac-fragments-the-highlands-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Fragments – The Highlands Children","date":"1296","desc":"The events of the novel take place in Scotland, following Fillan and his sister Ailéas during the country's invasion by the army of King Edward I of England in 1296, and it focuses on the local culture of the Highlands."},{"id":"ac-fragments-the-witches-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Fragments – The Witches of the Moors","date":"1609","desc":"At Bayonne, running within the Château-Vieux, Judge Pierre de Lancre held his documents and settled in to escape the heat."},{"id":"ac-fragments-the-blade-1","type":"roman","level":"bonus","tmdb":"0","media":"tv","title":"Assassin's Creed: Fragments – The Blade of Aizu","date":"1867-1868","desc":"Japan, 1868. The opposition between the Tokugawa Shogunate and the Emperor's supporters is growing under the influence of external forces. The Templars have infiltrated the Emperor's court and are pushing him to go to war against Tokugawa, an ally of the Assassin Brotherhood. Could the glorious era of the Samurai be on the verge of collapse? Atsuko, a 16-year-old Japanese girl, grew up in the wealthy neighborhoods of the city of Aizu."}]}]};
